  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-05-08T18:13:58.384Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello I'm dotsu. I have been playing VRC for a while now. Seeing some games that are open source or allow modifications to it like 7 days to die or a open source FPS the games have a way of a community who know how the games works and how to fix something for their situation. But with VRC I see a community who has a understanding of how it works but cant fix anything. If VRC where to go open source i think it would be nice. Not only would development go faster and such but also the community would feel involved and if need be a way to make it a official build would be needed to connect to the servers. If also maybe a P2P network could be done if the main way we connect through a dedicated server fails. Its an idea for VRC or if updating to the new version of unity works then that two. But the game i feel needs a way out of alpha and this may help.",
